node_modules/
.next/
dist/
.wrangler/
.env*
!.env.example
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
# data/ holds fetched copies of the registries, which are someone else's file
# and get re-fetched every build. The exceptions are inputs, not output: a
# measurement nobody can reproduce without an API budget, a survey read by hand
# off two dozen websites, the seam map read against a pinned harness tag, and
# the seat inventory. The site links to all four as its receipts —
# sponsors.json in particular MUST be committed, because dshthemes.com fetches
# it from this repo's raw URL and because /sponsor tells readers the seat's
# term dates are a matter of public record, and seams.json because the front
# page invites the reader to check the regex that produced every count on it.
data/*.json
!data/ecosystem.json
!data/directories.json
!data/seams.json
# and the installability census, which is the receipt for the one claim on the
# front page that is about other people's packages rather than our own rows.
!data/installability.json
!data/sponsors.json
.vinext/
